jobResponsibilities:
As an Organisation Excellence Manager, you will take on a portfolio of initiatives. Depending on organisational priorities and your experience, your responsibilities may include the following:

•	Corporate Planning and Organisational Strategy. Drive URA’s corporate planning process and work with Management in charting URA's strategic direction, translating priorities into corporate plans and ensuring alignment across the organisation. Organise management retreats and staff conferences;
•	Strategic sensing and coordination. Analyse developments in URA’s operating environment and coordinate cross-cutting Whole-of-Government and Ministry-level issues relevant to URA;
•	Organisation development and transformation. Identify and drive opportunities to improve how URA works, through strengthening both culture and our processes. Work with departments to improve processes, service delivery and organisational effectiveness, including through digitalisation, AI and business process redesign;
•	Enterprise performance and governance. Strengthen and implement URA’s governance frameworks, including Enterprise Risk Management (ERM), Business Continuity Management (BCM), incident management and Workplace Safety & Health;
•	Sustainability. Review URA's organisational ESG efforts and support the implementation of its ESG roadmap; and Board and Management governance. Support effective Board governance and providing secretariat support to the URA Board and Management. Support Board planning and development, including Board meetings, workshops, visits, renewal and related activities.

Climate action is a priority for MSE, and is driven by the Energy & Climate Policy Division (ECPD).  ECPD is MSE’s coordinating policy desk for issues overseen by the Inter-Ministerial Committee on Climate Change (IMCCC). ECPD drives policies relating to climate science, climate adaptation and climate mitigation, including issues such as carbon pricing, decarbonising Singapore’s economy, coastal protection, and reducing urban heat. You will join the Climate Mitigation team to help Singapore navigate an uneven and complex climate landscape, domestically and internationally.

As part of the Climate Mitigation team within ECPD, you will work with a diverse range of stakeholders from the public sector (e.g. NCCS, MTI and various statutory boards), private sector and civil society on a whole-of-nation effort to mitigate climate change. Amongst many other issues, you will be: 

•	Developing strategies to realise carbon abatement through adoption of a variety of low-carbon solutions,from scaling up international carbon markets to promoting energy efficiency nationally;
•	Reviewing the price of carbon; 
•	Reviewing and strengthening NEA’s capabilities to support low-carbon strategies, e.g. those in relation to NEA’s role as the carbon tax administrator and the national carbon accounting authority;
•	Developing thought leadership for international climate mitigation issues (e.g. scaling up innovative financing models to facilitate the low-carbon transition) in partnership with IMCCC agencies; and
•	Supporting inter-agency efforts in driving the triple transition of carbon, energy and economy.

