jobDescription:
This role is part of MHA’s Civilian Generalist career track. Learn more: https://go.gov.sg/civiliangeneralist

The Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) aspires to be a world-class organisation in delivering safety and security for our people. In pursuing our mission to make Singapore our Safe and Secure Best Home, we remain always constant and true to our core values of Honour and Unity. 

The Training and Competency Development Division (TCD) is MHA’s staff authority to ensure that training policies and plans are progressive and future-ready. It is responsible for charting the overall strategic direction for Home Team (HT) training policies including driving systematic and long-term strategy for skills and competency development for all HT officers as well as training capability development across the HT. TCD is also responsible for ensuring that MHQ officers have a seamless and meaningful training and learning (T&L) experience to ensure optimal training and learning.

As Senior Assistant Executive / Executive (Training and Competency Development), key responsibilities of the job holder include:
•	Plan and execute implementation of the training interventions as part of the upskilling roadmap for MHQ officers;
•	Streamline and automate statistics/information gathering, training administration processes and generation of training reports;
•	Take up deskhead duties for selected MHQ Divisions for more targeted engagement; 
•	Improve and continue to build up a culture of learning in MHA; and
•	Training coordination

jobResponsibilities:
