jobResponsibilities:
Brief description of Job Scope:

The First Responders Team in PSV attends to high-risk and cases require immediate response. Reporting to the Team Lead/Senior Manager, your role is to undertake crisis case management duties, immediate safety planning and intervention work for high-risk child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults experiencing violence, abuse or neglect cases. You will also support in developing operational processes, policies, systems and training for the team and work closely with the professional partners to ensure an effective protection system for them.

Responsibilities:

As a First Responder, you will:
•	Carry out statutory functions under the Children and Young Person Act, Women’s Charter and Vulnerable Adults Act in the protection of child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults cases such as conducting on-site response to emergency cases, issuance of Protector Power/ Emergency Order to ensure safety etc.  
•	Respond on-site to high-risk cases involving child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults, conduct safety assessment and implement immediate safety planning to ensure their safety, during and after-office hours;
•	Collaborate closely with the professional partners to ensure coordinated case management for the safety of the children, domestic violence survivors, vulnerable adults and their families; 
•	Develop and implement operational processes and policies to guide the team’s operations;
•	Work closely with the planning team to identify key competencies and trainings for the team; and
•	Identify and engage key professionals to collaborate and build up interface to facilitate a smooth service delivery.

The job scope involves:

•	Understanding and contextualising broader WOG transformation initiatives and efforts into specific initiatives for the Ministry’s transformation; 
•	Designing and driving organisational development initiatives
•	Facilitating business units to develop, translate and implement transformation initiatives; 
•	Organising MinLaw’s corporate events to achieve organisational development and innovation objectives
•	Secretariat for Minlaw’s transformation-related meetings

The Income Security Policy Division (ISPD) drives national efforts to empower Singaporeans in achieving greater financial security in retirement. Within ISPD, the Retirement System Department lead policies to help Singaporeans meet retirement, housing and healthcare needs through the Central Provident Fund (CPF) system. 

Your work will directly impact how Singapore’s evolving workforce, including platform workers and self-employed persons, build their retirement savings. You will also work closely with agencies such as CPF Board, Ministry of Finance (MOF), Ministry of Health (MOH), Ministry of National Development (MND) to shape policies affecting housing, healthcare, and retirement adequacy for Singaporeans. This role offers exposure to Singapore’s wider social security landscape, where you will learn to translate data insights into policies that balance competing priorities and public expectations.
You will have the opportunity to work on the following: 
• Analyse workforce trends and CPF contribution patterns to design retirement policies for Singapore's evolving workforce;
• Propose policy solutions, from behavioural nudges to government support, to better help platform workers and self-employed persons grow their retirement savings;
• Drive reviews to optimise the use of CPF savings for housing and healthcare needs, while safeguarding long-term retirement adequacy; 
• Oversee the full policy process from scheme design, stakeholder consultations to implementation and public comms; and
• Engage in efforts to streamline the collection of CPF contributions, so as to improve the employer and employee experience for businesses and Singaporeans.

You can also look forward to a collaborative and nurturing working environment, with supervisors supporting your career development.

jobRequirements:
•	Proven relevant experience as a Personal Assistant, or in a similar role supporting senior management; 
•	Able to work independently with good organisational and time-management skills to provide support in secretarial matters relating to assigned principal; 
•	Work with relevant stakeholders at various levels to obtain relevant inputs and ensure smooth coordination and transition between meetings and appointments; 
•	Professional and resilient, able to perform under pressure, manage short timelines and adapt to fast-paced environment with shifting priorities quickly.

jobResponsibilities:
You will be part of the Operations Policy and Planning team in POP to develop and implement operations policies and service models to improve services for vulnerable individuals and families. You will:
•	Develop and review operations policies and service models relating to the rehabilitation of offenders, protection of children and families from domestic violence, and/or gambling safeguards;
•	Implement new operations policies, service models, or legislative amendments in collaboration with RPG operational divisions;
•	Collaborate with policy directorate to ensure alignment between policy intent and operations policies;
•	Work closely with RPG operational divisions and stakeholders to identify gaps and propose solutions; 
•	Optimise limited resources to better protect the vulnerable and rehabilitate youth offenders.

jobRequirements:
The ideal candidate should be able to: 
•	Analyse gaps, emerging needs, cross-cutting issues, trade-offs and adopt mindset shifts to propose solutions;
•	Drive and project manage initiatives to ensure timely implementation;
•	Develop and review funding and service models with clear strategies to achieve service goals;
•	Clearly and concisely articulate strategies and proposals;
•	Work well together other RPG and MSF divisions; 
